Z||000001||BroCar 87||08-27-2000||08:40 PM||||V8Fiero... take a look at EUROWORKS, They were gonna sponsor one of my fieros if I decided to race it. I wrote them an email and they got back to me in the next day or two. I recently wrote back to them but haven't heard anything... I may have to call down there. <BR>The sponsorship deal was with the "Mirage K" <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/8482/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/8482/index.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000002||86se/lambo||08-28-2000||12:14 AM||||i'm building an ifg countach as we speak. next week i will be picking the car up from ifg and can then talk more about the quality of their workmanship and tech support. as far as price goes they are very competitive.  for me i wanted the authentic replica of the 25th anniv. edition and ifg is down to the cm. before i sent my fiero to them my boys and i worked on the car for a few years and i really appreciate the fiero now as a stand alone sports car,it was heart wrenching to take off all the body panels,(now i want an 88). ihave read countless kit car magazines over the last 5 years and some companys seem to come and go. visit the shop,talk to the people and shop around. i live in CA, so ifg was also more convienent. feel freee to e-mail or post and i can let you know more as i experience it.<BR>mike<BR>86se||||reg||1
